# {{title}}

{{description}}

A sandboxed EmDash plugin for astro-cms, generated by `astro-cms plugin new`.

```bash
npm install
npm run check      # typecheck, validate the manifest, run the tests, build
```

## Use it on a site

1. Add it to the site: `"{{slug}}": "file:plugins/{{slug}}"` in `package.json`.
2. Import it in `astro.config.mjs`, then list it in `emdash({ sandboxed: [...] })`.
3. In the Dockerfile, build it (`cd plugins/{{slug}} && npm install && npm run build`) and copy `dist`, `package.json` and `emdash-plugin.jsonc` into the runtime image. `migration-guard` shows the pattern.

Before extending it, read `skills/creating-plugins/SKILL.md` (EmDash's rules) and `skills/creating-plugins/ASTRO-CMS.md` (our lessons).
